nces the first is the  school color which are reflected in the  clothing the player can wear as well as  the accessories that outfit the picnics  they take their Pokemon on orange for  scarlet and purple for Violet while both  games allow you to pick from four outfit  variations for each of the seasons  spring summer fall and winter the color  schemes for each outfit are respective  of the version you've picked and cannot  be changed you can buy accessories like  shoes and gloves however that do have a  variety of colors to pick from the other  major difference between Naranja and UVA  academies are the contents of the books  within their libraries and as a result  the law of paldea that you can learn  which pertains to the final major  difference between the two games before  you continue with the video I want to  warn you that the final difference  between scarlet and violet pertains to  late and end game content so if you  don't wish to learn about it consider  pausing this video and continuing it  later something that was apparent in the  lead up to scarlet and the violet was  that the games were themed around the  past and the future respectively this  was clear from the designs of the two  legendaries Corydon and miraidon as well  as the clothing of the two version  exclusive professors Sara and turo also  Sada comes from the Spanish word for  past Pasada and Toro comes from the  Spanish word for future futuro those  past and future Aesthetics play into  Paradox forms variants of Pokemon  separate from Regional variants like  palday and Woopa and Tauros with scarlet  and violet having their own exclusives  these Paradox forms are described in the  books of the library in naranha and UVA  academies hence why the content of the  book stiffers depending on the game  you're playing each of the Paradox forms  have a two words name which serves as  the name of the Pokemon itself for  example Scarlet's Paradox form Don fan  is known as great Tusk while Violet's  Para